        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): use Object.hasOwn instead of in operator in printSessionUpdate",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `printSessionUpdate` helper in `src/acp/client.ts:75` uses the `in` operator to check for `sessionUpdate` on the notification update object. The `in` operator traverses the prototype chain, so it would match inherited properties — though unlikely in practice, `Object.hasOwn()` is the more correct semantic for own-property checks.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/acp/client.ts`** — replace `!(\"sessionUpdate\" in update)` with `!Object.hasOwn(update, \"sessionUpdate\")` (1 line)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest — 54/54 passed including 3 new Object.hasOwn discriminator tests\n\n```bash\nnode node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run src/acp/client.test.ts\n```\n\n```\n ✓ printSessionUpdate discriminator check > Object.hasOwn correctly identifies sessionUpdate own-property on ACP SessionNotification updates 1ms\n ✓ printSessionUpdate discriminator check > Object.hasOwn correctly rejects non-sessionUpdate notifications 1ms\n ✓ printSessionUpdate discriminator check > Object.hasOwn rejects prototype-injected sessionUpdate (unlike 'in' operator) 1ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  54 passed (54)\n```\n\n### Real ACP SDK proof — @agentclientprotocol/sdk SessionNotification types\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/proof-99363-printSessionUpdate.mjs\n```\n\n```\nResults: 10 passed, 0 failed out of 10 assertions\n✅ PROOF PASSED — Object.hasOwn behavior is correct for ACP session updates.\n```\n\n## Related\n\nN/A (self-contained code hygiene improvement)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
